// NeoSoundFonts sets voice_oohs: a male voice singing "ooh" (stack it for a small choir). Samples: Simone Piervergili, NeoSoundFonts (Voice Oohs, Old Steel Guitar, Bamboo Flute), CC0 1.0 (https://github.com/NeoSoundFonts).
// Generated by scripts/make_neosound_library.py; sample paths are relative to the library's cache folder.
<control>
// volume: the median plain-velocity sample (loudest 400 ms) is -20 LUFS, its peak at most 0.7; dynamic layers keep their recorded levels.
<group> volume=-7 ampeg_release=0.4
<region> lokey=44 hikey=51 pitch_keycenter=47 lovel=1 hivel=127 seq_length=3 seq_position=1 sample=oohs/samples/Voice Oohs b2 rr1.wav
<region> lokey=44 hikey=51 pitch_keycenter=47 lovel=1 hivel=127 seq_length=3 seq_position=2 sample=oohs/samples/Voice Oohs b2 rr2.wav
<region> lokey=44 hikey=51 pitch_keycenter=47 lovel=1 hivel=127 seq_length=3 seq_position=3 offset=119 sample=oohs/samples/Voice Oohs b2 rr3.wav
